# Customer Checkout Redesign — All Verticals + Trades 3-Step + Split

## Context

The user uploaded 6 mockups (`attached_assets/*_customer_payment_page_*.png`, `customer_split_payment_page_*.png`, 2026-07-11) replacing the current blue/cyan HPP design with the brand-wide navy language: off-white `#F4F4F4` page, centered rounded navy `#040D6D` card, serif "tapt**pay**" wordmark, sky-blue `#58ABFF` text, huge amount figure. These tokens already exist in `client/src/lib/trades-theme.ts`. Beyond the restyle, trades gets a new **one-page animated 3-step flow** for quotes with deposits, replacing the separate quote-response page.

**Confirmed with user:** restyle applies to all verticals; trades 3 steps animate on ONE page (view quote → confirm [+ QR icon that re-opens quote PDF] → pay deposit); no deposit → just the payment step; "view quote" and the QR button both open the existing quote PDF; split redesign is restyle-only (behavior unchanged); merchant `customLogoUrl` still replaces the wordmark; the expanded "enter credit card ∨" panel is **sky blue**.

## Mockup spec (per page)

- **Retail/hospo**: label ("lunch"), `$25.00`, dark Google Pay pill, footer link "enter credit card ∨" → sky-blue expanding card panel.
- **Property**: address title, `$650`, subtitle "weekly rent payment", same pay controls.
- **Trades step 1**: title "deck replacement", FULL amount `$2,500`, subtitle "10% deposit required", single outline "view quote" button.
- **Trades step 2**: same info; button row animates to outline "confirm" + small square QR-icon button (re-opens quote PDF).
- **Trades step 3**: deposit amount `$250`, subtitle "10% deposit of $2,500", GPay + card link — this layout alone serves deposit-less trades invoices.
- **Split**: chip "Person 1 of 2", label, amount, circular − N + stepper, "enter amount" input, outline "confirm".

## Key facts (verified in code)

- `client/src/pages/checkout.tsx` (1659 lines) is the single HPP for retail (`/checkout/:transactionId`) and property/trades invoices (`/r/:token`); `isInvoice = !!token` (line 74), endpoints switch at 87–91, `payId` at 91. Styles are inline `CSSProperties` constants at 1468–1651.
- Wallet pre-sessions require `transaction?.id && payId` — in quote mode neither exists until confirm, so **swapping in the deposit-invoice token mid-page is safe**; sessions are created fresh afterward. No hard navigation needed.
- `/trades/quote/:token` (App.tsx:352) → `client/src/pages/trades/quote-response.tsx` (50 lines); fetches `GET /api/trades/quotes/token/:token` (routes.ts:6738 — marks quote `viewed` on first GET), responds via `POST .../respond` (routes.ts:6766 — on accept creates a `deposit`/`full` `job_invoice`, returns `depositInvoice` incl. `token` + `paymentUrl`; 409 already-responded, 410 expired). PDF at routes.ts:6712. This URL is baked into emails/SMS (`server/trades-delivery.ts:74`) and the quote PDF (`server/trades-quote-pdf.ts:163`) — keep it.
- Route param trap: `/trades/quote/:token` fills the same `token` param checkout.tsx reads — quote mode must treat it as the QUOTE token and not let it reach `isInvoice`/resolve.
- Resolve gaps (server work needed): `GET /api/checkout/resolve/:token` (routes.ts:6058) returns no `frequency` (property subtitle), no quote info (deposit subtitle), and auto-created deposit invoices have null `jobDetails` → description would show "Job invoice" instead of "deck replacement". Quote GET returns no invoice token for already-accepted quotes (needed for revisit → jump to step 3).
- Larken fonts: `client/public/assets/fonts/LarkenDEMO-Black.otf` + `BlackItalic.otf`; `@font-face` only in `landing.css:7–8` (weight 900 only) — checkout must load its own copy.
- `framer-motion@11` already a dep (used in `page-transition.tsx`). `playwright@1.60` available for screenshots. Mock mode: `client/src/mocks/mock-api.ts` covers transactions/resolve/merchant/windcave-env but NOT quote tokens (extend it).
- Property frequency source: `invoices_rent_requests.scheduleId → active_schedules.frequency` (`weekly|fortnightly|monthly`, schema.ts:802).

