### Stage 4 — Trades quote mode (3-step animated page)
- `App.tsx`: `/trades/quote/:token` → `<Checkout quoteMode />`; delete `pages/trades/quote-response.tsx`.
- `checkout.tsx`: `quoteMode` prop; `quoteToken = params.token` in quote mode; `const [acceptedInvoiceToken, setAcceptedInvoiceToken] = useState<string|null>(null)`; effective `token = quoteMode ? acceptedInvoiceToken ?? undefined : params.token` so all downstream wiring is untouched. New quote `useQuery` (same endpoint quote-response used). Steps:
  1. `quote-view`: title = first line-item description, amount = `totalCents`, subtitle "`{depositValue}`% deposit required" (fixed → "deposit required"; none → "quote total"); outline "view quote" → `window.open` PDF; mark viewed (also start at step 2 if `quote.viewedAt` set).
  2. `quote-confirm`: framer-motion `layout` animates the button row → "confirm" + square QR-icon button (re-opens PDF); subtle "decline" text link underneath (endpoint supports it; mockups omit it — flag to user).
  3. Confirm → POST respond → `setAcceptedInvoiceToken(depositInvoice.token)` + `history.replaceState(null,"","/r/"+token)`; `AnimatePresence mode="wait"` crossfades card content to the standard payment layout; wallet pre-sessions init fresh (verified safe). No-deposit quotes: confirm → full-amount invoice, same transition.
  - Revisit accepted link → jump to step 3 via Stage-3 `invoice` field (or already-paid state); declined/expired (409/410/status) → styled terminal states.
  - Gate the `!payId` "Invalid payment link" early-return (~1073) behind quote mode. Optionally extract steps 1–2 presentation to `client/src/components/checkout/quote-steps.tsx`; card shell + step 3 stay in checkout.tsx so the card never remounts.
- Extend `mock-api.ts`: quote token GET + respond POST returning a fake resolvable `depositInvoice.token`.

Check (mock): full 3-step animation; QR button re-opens PDF; URL becomes `/r/<token>`; revisit jumps to step 3. Real-mode: create quote → open emailed link → accept → verify quote status + deposit invoice in DB, `/r/:token` standalone.

